Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/tags/xtif_dir.c
Line: 78
Function: _XTIFFPrintDirectory
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: fprintf uses "%lu" to print xd->xd_example_single (uint32_t). On LP64 platforms where unsigned long is 64-bit, this varargs type mismatch causes fprintf to read 8 bytes from the stack while only 4 were provided, leading to an out-of-bounds stack read and potential information leak or crash.

Source context:
```c
